 "description": "Malayalam verses numbered differently from the KJV numbering that the Hebrew and Greek (STEPBible) data follow. Each key is a Malayalam book:chapter:verse; the value is the KJV verse it corresponds to, or a list when one Malayalam verse holds two KJV verses. Verses not listed have the same number in both. Used by scripts/align-malayalam.mjs to pair each Malayalam verse with its original words, and written into the database (table verse_map) so the app shows the right Hebrew or Greek under each Malayalam verse. Found by comparing the Malayalam and KJV verse lists chapter by chapter and reading the verses either side of each difference. The Malayalam title of Psalm 146 has no Hebrew counterpart and is left unmapped. The WEB key: the WEB places the doxology of Romans (KJV 16:25-27) at 14:24-26. TAM: the Tamil IRV numbers like the KJV except 3 John, where the KJV's verse 14 is its verses 14 and 15. HIN: the Hindi IRV numbers like the KJV except 3 John, split as in the Tamil, and Revelation 12:18, which is the first words of the KJV's 13:1 (\"And I stood upon the sand of the sea\"). IRV: the Malayalam IRV numbers like the KJV except 3 John and Revelation 12:18, as the Hindi IRV. OMCV: the Open Malayalam Contemporary Version numbers like the KJV except 3 John, split as in the Tamil. Both join a few verses into one sentence (\\v 17-18): the first holds the KJV verses it joins, and the others are written as joined to it.",
